// A type declared OUTSIDE the cycle and mirrored by TWO co-tenants of the
// merged package. Nothing here is an existential; this file exists for the
// alias-collision arm alone.
//
// A mirror is named by a Go ALIAS — `type NomiT_Stamp = nomimodN.NomiT_Stamp`
// (foreign.go's qualifyGoName) — and that alias used to be deduplicated per
// GEN, which is one FILE, while the Go package it was written into was one
// strongly-connected COMPONENT. So two co-tenants mirroring this one type wrote
// the declaration twice into one package: `NomiT_Stamp redeclared in this block`.
//
// MEASURED as four Go compile failures on `tests/15-app-and-defer/effects/`,
// whose `dev`/`prod`/`test` co-tenants each mirror `log.ProdLogger`,
// `console.StdConsole` and `clocks.FakeClock` from outside their component. It
// was unreachable until those files stopped being refused, so it was latent
// rather than absent — and it is nothing to do with interfaces, which is why it
// needs its own arm here rather than riding on `App`.
//
// This file must NOT import a cycle member, or it joins the component and there
// is no cross-package alias left to collide.
pub struct Stamp {
    s: String
}

pub fn stamp(s: String): Stamp {
    Stamp{s}
}
